{#- B-2 section introduction: one per zone (worked example, section 2).
    Every argument that prints a value is a slot placeholder from
    b2_narrative.Writer; code fills it. Arguments ending in _n are plain numbers
    used only to choose wording, and are never printed. The literal text holds
    no digits and no number words. A line starting "- " is a bullet. -#}

{% macro intro(checkpoints, checkpoints_n, samples, samples_n) -%}
This zone covers {{ checkpoints }} checkpoint{{ "" if checkpoints_n == 1 else "s" }} and {% if samples_n %}recorded {{ samples }} sample{{ "" if samples_n == 1 else "s" }} during the run.{% else %}was not sampled during the run.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro mean(field, mean, usable, usable_n, excluded, excluded_n, rank, rank_n, ranked, joint, total) -%}
- Mean {{ field }} here was {{ mean }}, across {{ usable }} usable sample{{ "" if usable_n == 1 else "s" }}{% if excluded_n %} ({{ excluded }} excluded){% endif %}{% if ranked %}; the {{ "joint " if joint else "" }}{% if rank_n == 1 %}highest{% else %}{{ rank }} highest{% endif %} of the {{ total }} zones where it could be computed{% endif %}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro no_mean(field, excluded, excluded_n) -%}
- No {{ field }} mean: none of the zone's samples were usable{% if excluded_n %} (all {{ excluded }} excluded){% endif %}.
{%- endmacro %}
